<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Nov 30.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Nov 30.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Nov 30.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   220	   0.28     380950  83.81     6.64</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   154	   0.19     457800  70.50     6.43</p>
<p>Reliance	     181	   0.16     220550  39.92     4.61</p>
<p>ACC		   1005	   0.98	28290  28.43     5.08</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    315	   0.31	79650  25.09     5.13</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    215	   0.10	80300  17.26     2.43</p>
<p>Tata Power	   107	   0.10     158450  16.95     4.87</p>
<p>Gujarat Amb Cem    215	   0.20	59400  12.77     4.85</p>
<p>G.E.Shipping	  28.5	 0.03     229900   6.55     5.49</p>
<p>ICICI		   52	   0.04     122750   6.38     4.01</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 5.52 percent on an annualised basis against 4.96 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Nov 23.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
